l i don't know it's not the  kind of thing these guys are writing  about they're writing about  much more mundane things this is a much  more complicated thing to understand  takes much more effort it's really not  the  the kind of thing and the kinds of  things that are being written about are  much more  uh frankly much more straightforward and  much require much less effort on the  part of the science journalist  you know why it's evolved that way i'm  not really sure i think it's a shame  and perhaps it's related to my previous  complaint so to speak  about people's unwillingness to try to  actually explain science  to people at large and uh in a sense i'm  i'm trying to do my small part here uh  with these live streams  to uh to try and explain some things  that i  know something about in a way that i  hope people  can uh can understand and relate to  and uh you know more people should do  this stuff  anyway unfortunately i have to wrap this  up here  and um as i said my next few weeks are  very dominated by these educational  activities that we have every summer  and um probably this particular  um uh  series about um history of science and  technology  is probably going to be on hiatus for  the next four weeks  although we will be doing a variety of  live streams which may include some  about history of  of science and technology as part of our  summer school and summer camp and um  uh maybe somebody knows that schedule  i'm afraid i don't yet know it  um but uh look forward to  people joining us uh for some of those  um  uh live streams and um  uh i hope um  you found this interesting and um i find  it interesting to try and explain things  and um i look forward to seeing you all  another time  alright bye for now
 

